# Prettier + commit before PRs

When the user asks to create a PR (or push and create a PR):

1. Run Prettier on every source file you changed (`pnpm exec prettier --write <paths>`). Then `pnpm exec prettier --check .` (or `pnpm run format:check`) and fix any reported files.
2. If the working tree is dirty, **commit** those changes (including format-only fixes). Do not open a PR with uncommitted work.
3. Only then push and create the PR.

Do not skip this because files “look formatted.” CI fails on `format:check`.

Do not run `prettier --write .` unless format:check reports files you did not just edit — then write **only** those paths.
